* litdiscover.pkg
*
* Stata package description file for litdiscover.
* Read by `net describe litdiscover` and used to drive `net install
* litdiscover` from this repository. See [R] net for the file format
* specification.
*
* File-line conventions:
*   d ...    description lines (free text, the first becomes the title)
*   f file   install file 'file'; its destination is decided by suffix
*   F file   install file 'file' into the system directories regardless
*            of its suffix (used here for the Python helpers, the
*            example dataset, and the user-facing Markdown documentation,
*            which Stata would otherwise not know how to route)

v 3
d 'LITDISCOVER': module for theory-aware literature review and discovery
d
d litdiscover combines latent Dirichlet allocation (LDA) topic
d modelling of abstract text with a deductive overlay of researcher-
d coded construct fields (theory, dependent variable, independent
d variable, moderator, mediator, decision, context, method, journal,
d year). It produces topic-by-field cross-tabulations, TCCM and ADO
d framework outputs, network-analytic measures (degree, betweenness,
d Louvain communities, modularity) over construct co-occurrences,
d FREX exclusivity scores, per-topic stability diagnostics via
d Jaccard similarity across random seeds, UMass coherence diagnostics,
d and a suite of static figures and interactive HTML deliverables
d (pyLDAvis, pyvis, plotly Sankey) suitable for systematic literature
d reviews in social sciences, management, marketing, and adjacent fields.
d
d The short-form alias litdi forwards every argument to litdiscover.
d
d KW: literature review
d KW: topic modelling
d KW: latent Dirichlet allocation
d KW: LDA
d KW: bibliometrics
d KW: TCCM
d KW: ADO
d KW: FREX
d KW: network analysis
d KW: text analysis
d
d Requires: Stata version 19.5
d Requires: Python 3.10 or later configured for Stata (see help python)
d Requires (figures option): SSC packages heatplot, palettes, colrspace
d Requires (Python): pandas, numpy, scikit-learn, scipy, networkx
d Requires (Python, figures): matplotlib, seaborn, wordcloud
d Requires (Python, interactive): pyLDAvis, pyvis, plotly
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260517
d
d Author: Nebojsa S. Davcik
d Affiliation: EM Normandie Business School, Oxford, UK
d Email: davcik@live.com
d ORCID: 0000-0003-1041-8788
d
d Licence: GPL-3.0-or-later
d Repository: https://github.com/Davcik/litdiscover

f litdiscover.ado
f litdi.ado
f litdiscover.sthlp
F litdiscover.py
F litdiscover_net.py
F litdiscover_viz.py
F litdiscover_example500.dta
